{"blocks":[{"type":"voiceover","audio_files":["lesson_30/lesson_30_seg_01.mp3"],"total_audio_seconds":93.02,"timed_text":[{"start_s":0,"text":"Day 30, you made it."},{"start_s":2.54,"text":"You don't want to gloss over that, okay?"},{"start_s":5.22,"text":"Most people quit around Day 8 or 15, when it starts feeling like work."},{"start_s":12.58,"text":"But you kept showing up every single day and that is not a small thing."},{"start_s":17.98,"text":"Think about where you were when you started this, what you didn't have yet."},{"start_s":22.46,"text":"No reset word, no If-Then plan, no evidence log, no traffic light system."},{"start_s":38.04,"text":"No connection to your why."},{"start_s":40.64,"text":"You have all of that now."},{"start_s":42.44,"text":"Not because someone gave it to you — you built it, rep by rep, day by day."},{"start_s":50.08,"text":"The question to carry forward: the one that keeps athletes growing."},{"start_s":60.76,"text":"Not how much did I improve, what's the next step?"},{"start_s":64.62,"text":"Take it into every season, every competition, every time you plateau."},{"start_s":70.72,"text":"Move forward."},{"start_s":72.86,"text":"Before you journal — go back to your Day 23 visualization and read it."},{"start_s":80.78,"text":"Sit inside that moment again. Then read your evidence log — every entry."},{"start_s":87.82,"text":"See what you've already done."},{"start_s":89.8,"text":"Then come back and write your last entry."}]},{"type":"prompt_cards","ambient_audio":"ambient/ambient_music.mp3","cards":[{"intro_hold_seconds":0,"prompt":"Open your Day 23 journal entry — your five to ten year visualization. Read it. Let yourself feel it again.","min_entry_seconds":0,"journal_link":{"kind":"program_day","program_day":23}},{"intro_hold_seconds":0,"prompt":"Now open your evidence log. Read every entry from the beginning.","min_entry_seconds":0,"journal_link":{"kind":"session_entries"}},{"intro_hold_seconds":0,"prompt":"The distance between that visualization and where you stand right now? That's the work. And you've already started closing it.","min_entry_seconds":0},{"intro_hold_seconds":0,"prompt":"What's next?","min_entry_seconds":0}],"summary":{"display":"all","header":"","hold_seconds":0}},{"type":"voiceover","audio_files":["lesson_30/lesson_30_seg_02.mp3"],"total_audio_seconds":41.59,"timed_text":[{"start_s":0,"text":"You don't need a score to know what changed."},{"start_s":2.76,"text":"You know it in how you showed up, how you handled the last competition."},{"start_s":14.86,"text":"That's the evidence."},{"start_s":16.66,"text":"Keep the log, run the routine, use the tools, build on your why."},{"start_s":24.92,"text":"When it gets hard, you've been here before and came out with a plan."},{"start_s":35.4,"text":"Programs complete, but the training is it."},{"start_s":38.82,"text":"Go compete like it."},{"start_s":40.32,"text":"Stay relentless."}]},{"type":"journal_prompt","prompt":"What is different about the way you think about competing now compared to where you started? What does the next chapter look like — and what's your first move?"}]}
